IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`
IMPORT `rta-s55`
IMPORT `rta-dates`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — GOAL 5: THE TRIBUNAL.
--
--   "Is this application to the Tribunal in time, and within its monetary
--    limit; and how much may it award for an unlawful act?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_120.txt — ss 54, 77,
-- 108, 109, 109B-109C.

§ `Goal 5 — the Tribunal`

-- s 77 "(5) ... the Tribunal does not have jurisdiction to require any party
-- to pay any sum ... in excess of $100,000. (5A) Subsection (5) shall not
-- prevent a party from abandoning so much of a claim as exceeds $100,000".
-- (4) the recovery of premises is "regardless of the value".
@ref s 77(5)-(5A)
GIVEN claim IS A NUMBER, abandoned IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal has jurisdiction over a claim of` claim `, excess abandoned` abandoned IF
    claim AT MOST 100000 OR abandoned

-- s 54(3) "If the tenant makes the application within 28 working days after
-- receiving the termination notice, the tenant may at the same time apply for
-- an order declaring the notice to be of no effect."
@ref s 54(3)
GIVEN received IS A DATE, cal IS A `Local calendar`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to seek a no-effect order against a retaliatory notice received on` received `, calendar` cal MEANS
    `the` 28 `th working day after` received `, calendar` cal

-- s 108(7) "After the expiration of 12 months from the date of a work order,
-- it shall not be enforced without the leave of the Tribunal."
@ref s 108(7)
GIVEN ordered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day a work order may be enforced without leave, ordered` ordered MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`add years` ordered 1)

-- s 109 "(2) A landlord or a tenant may not apply under subsection (1) later
-- than— (a) 12 months after the termination of the tenancy in the case of—
-- (i) an unlawful act to which section 19(2) refers; or (ii) a failure to
-- keep records in respect of bonds that is an unlawful act to which section
-- 30(2) refers; or (b) 12 months after the date of commission of the unlawful
-- act in the case of any other unlawful act. (2A) The chief executive may not
-- apply ... later than 12 months after the date on which the chief executive
-- first became aware of the unlawful act." NOTHING: under (2)(a) the tenancy
-- has not ended, so time has not begun to run.
@ref s 109(2)-(2A)
GIVEN a IS AN `Unlawful act application`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the unextended last day to apply about the unlawful act` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `applicant`
    WHEN `the chief executive` THEN
        CONSIDER a's `chief executive first aware on`
        WHEN JUST aware THEN JUST (`add years` aware 1)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 109(2A) runs from when the chief executive became aware`
    OTHERWISE
        IF   a's `an unlawful act under s 19(2) or a bond-records failure under s 30(2)`
        THEN CONSIDER a's `tenancy terminated on`
             WHEN JUST ended THEN JUST (`add years` ended 1)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`add years` (a's `unlawful act committed on`) 1)

`s 109(2A) runs from when the chief executive became aware` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 109(2A): the chief executive's time runs from the day they first became aware of the unlawful act, which is not given"

@ref s 109(2)-(2A)
GIVEN a IS AN `Unlawful act application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unlawful act application is in time` a IF
    CONSIDER `the last day to apply about the unlawful act` a
    WHEN JUST last THEN a's `unlawful act application made on` AT MOST last
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 109 "(3) If ... the Tribunal is satisfied that the person ... committed
-- the unlawful act intentionally, and that, having regard to [intent, effect,
-- the interests of the other party and the public interest] it would be just
-- ..., the Tribunal may make an order accordingly. (3A) In the case of ... an
-- unlawful act under section 54(6), the Tribunal may order the landlord to pay
-- ... if ... satisfied that it is just to do so having regard to the matters
-- referred to in subsection (3)(b) to (d). (4) The maximum amount ... is the
-- amount shown opposite that section in column 3 of [Schedule 1A]."
@ref s 109(1)-(4); Schedule 1A
@export The most the Tenancy Tribunal may award as exemplary damages for an unlawful act under s 109 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): if the application is in time and the act was intentional (not needed for a retaliatory notice under s 54(6)) and an award is just, the amount sought up to the Schedule 1A maximum for that act; otherwise 0. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS AN `Unlawful act application`  @desc Who applies, the kind of unlawful act, when it was committed, when the tenancy ended, when the chief executive became aware, the application date, intent, whether it is a retaliatory notice, whether an award is just, the amount sought and the Schedule 1A maximum
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Tribunal may award for the unlawful act` a MEANS
    IF       `the unlawful act application is in time` a
         AND (a's `committed intentionally` OR a's `a retaliatory notice under s 54(6)`)
         AND a's `just to award exemplary damages`
    THEN min (a's `exemplary damages sought`) (a's `Schedule 1A maximum for the act`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 109C "The maximum amount of pecuniary penalty for an unlawful act referred
-- to in section 109B is $50,000." s 109B(1)(a) the landlord had 6 or more
-- tenancies or a boarding house; (2) the chief executive applies within 12
-- months after first becoming aware.
@ref ss 109B(1)(a), (2), 109C
GIVEN tenancies IS A NUMBER, boarding IS A BOOLEAN, sought IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most pecuniary penalty for a landlord of` tenancies `tenancies, a boarding house landlord` boarding `, sought` sought MEANS
    IF   tenancies AT LEAST 6 OR boarding
    THEN min sought 50000
    ELSE 0

-- Legislation Act 2019 s 55 (applied 2026-10-17 at the user's direction).
@ref s 109(2)-(2A); Legislation Act 2019 s 55
@export The last day to apply to the Tenancy Tribunal about an unlawful act under s 109 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): for a landlord or tenant, 12 months after the tenancy ends for a bond receipt, lodging or records failure (none yet while it continues), and 12 months after the act for any other; for the chief executive, 12 months after first becoming aware of it; a last day that is not a working day runs to the next working day (Legislation Act 2019 s 55). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS AN `Unlawful act application`  @desc Who applies, the kind of unlawful act, when it was committed, when the tenancy ended, when the chief executive became aware, the application date, intent, whether it is a retaliatory notice, whether an award is just, the amount sought and the Schedule 1A maximum
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to apply about the unlawful act` a MEANS
    `the last day under s 55, if any, for a deadline of` (`the unextended last day to apply about the unlawful act` a)
